# Line endings are LF everywhere: in the object store and in the working tree.
#
# Without this file, Git honors each contributor's core.autocrlf. On Windows
# that is commonly true, so a checkout materializes CRLF while .editorconfig
# declares end_of_line = lf and Prettier enforces it. The repository's own
# linter then contradicts itself on that platform: ./scripts/lint-files.sh
# reports a style failure for every text file, and its --fix pass rewrites the
# whole tree to LF, which leaves several hundred files listed as modified even
# though no content changed. CI never sees this because CI runs on Linux.
#
# text=auto keeps Git's binary detection, so only files Git considers text are
# converted. eol=lf is what pins the working-tree side on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
